{#
  Purpose:    Generate ONE batch (3–4 sections) of the Functional Specification Document (FSD).
              Produces structured text with section markers parsed by document_builder.py.
              Called once per batch — never for the whole document in one call (CLAUDE.md §3.7).
  Variables:
    - structured_summary (dict): keys: requirements, kpis, data_sources, domain, key_entities, open_gaps
    - technology (str): selected SAP technology
    - clarification_answers (dict): {question_id: answer_text} — may be empty
    - metadata (dict): consultant, client, project, engagement_code
    - all_section_titles (list[str]): "N. Title" for every section in the document, for context
    - batch_sections (list[dict]): the subset of sections to generate in this call —
      each item has: number, title, description, format
    - section_instructions (dict): {section_number: detailed writing instructions}
    - locked_context (str): optional plain-text content of sections already locked via the
      interactive loop before "Skip Review — Generate Full FSD Now" handed the remaining
      sections to this batch generator. Empty string on a cold-start batch run.
  Output:     Structured text with ## SECTION_N: markers, one per section in batch_sections.
#}
